From 94d2718a8174a4b63af99a359f9bbb765aef325b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bedrock): join offline LAN worlds

Probe NetherNet and RakNet on the local network and show compatible worlds in a separate account-free screen. Parse the retail 1.26.51 NetherNet layout 7 advertisement so authentication flags and the nonce come from the host instead of LAN assumptions.

For self-signed worlds, create one identity before the NetherNet offer and pass the same token to ViaBedrock login. Keep the selected transport, responder, network ID, nonce, and login mode on the connection. RakNet pongs have no auth flags, so the screen requires an explicit offline-login choice for those worlds.

Receive complete NetherNet signaling datagrams and repair iOS LAN answers that omit trailing SDP attributes from their declared length. Otherwise the client can time out before the ICE connection opens even though discovery succeeded.

Place the LAN subtitle and world list immediately beneath the VFP logo. This screen has no search bar or tabs, so the extra header space obscured the list.

Use core AuthData.createSelfSigned for LAN and account-free HTTP offers.
Transfer the exact pre-handshake token and key independently of LAN
metadata, and preserve them for game login. Exact offline BDS1.26.51.1
rejects unsigned HTTP offers but opens the signed self identity transport.
Online account tokens retain their existing path.

Label the server browser button Bedrock LAN Worlds so users can distinguish native discovery from the Java LAN list.

Preserve RakNet channel construction, packet framing, status queries, and
encryption for local LAN fixtures alongside explicit HTTP NetherNet.
Upstream now defaults ordinary Bedrock addresses to HTTP and removed the
RakNet infrastructure. The LAN feature retains its transport ownership
and registers its browser in the current Server Lists popup.
